  "starterCode": "# Sandwich Norm — reconstructed educational contract\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef solution(x, scale=1.0, eps=1e-5):\n    # TODO: implement the operation described in the problem statement\n    pass\n",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Sandwich Norm** by following direct architectural principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\ndef solution(x, scale=1.0, eps=1e-5):\n    x=np.asarray(x,dtype=float)\n    def norm(z): return z/np.sqrt(np.mean(z*z,axis=-1,keepdims=True)+eps)\n    return (norm(x)*scale).tolist()\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the primary sequence length or dimension.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
